// The Water Zombie: look() for shape 872.
//
// WHY THIS CLASS IS PINNED TO 872. The engine picks the usecode class for
// an item's events from its SHAPE NUMBER (item.cpp:1516), and a monster is
// an item: a double-click on one runs look() in the class equal to its
// shape. The Lake's eggs hatch shape 872 (build_map_10.py, lv_shapes
// SHAPE_MON_ZOMBIE) since Douglas picked its art on 2026-10-11
// (docs/art-track.md contract 9), and retail EUSECODE has no class there,
// so without this one the monster would say nothing where the ghoul it
// replaces said "ghoul". `lv_manifest.json` pins TYPEWATERZOMBIE to 872.
//
// THE CLASS IS THE RETAIL GHOUL'S, renamed: GHOUL (class 142) has look()
// alone and barks its name, and nothing else of a monster's behaviour lives
// in usecode (its stats are the u8monsters.ini row, its animation the
// ANIM.DAT entry). The name is the one the 1994 dialogue uses: Ezrekal's
// "undead water zombies" (lv-patched/EZREKAL.UNK).

uses "item";

typeclass TypeWaterZombie inherits Item
{
	process look();
}

process TypeWaterZombie::look()
{
	bark("water zombie");
}
